  "query_preview": "..\nA fairly large upper low off the California coast will keep an \ninduced ridge to its east, allowing NE MT to experience dry \nconditions and warmer than normal temps through Friday.\n\nBut the upper low will merge with southern oriented jet stream \nand move into Montana Friday. This will pull up pacific moisture \nfrom the Desert SW while a surface low developing over southern MT\npulls NE tracking showers across the CWA through Saturday morning.\nThis will also allow NW winds to increase late Friday behind a \ncold front. The showers are expected to exit the CWA Saturday \nwith significantly cooler high temps Saturday onward.\n\nRough conditions on Fort Peck Lake can be expected beginning\nFriday afternoon through Saturday afternoon. Check the forecast \nif you have plans to visit the area later this week.\n\nRainfall amounts still look to be greatest over the NW half of \nthe CWA with the total amount expected to be around a quarter \ninch or less.\n\nBeyond Saturday, temps look to remain below normal as an upper\nridge early next week doen't nudge east of the Pac NW.\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo changes to NBM. \n\nConfidence is High through Thursday night.\n\nConfidence is Moderate Friday through Saturday night. \n\nConfidence is low from Sunday onward as ensembles go out of \nphase.\n\nTFJ/GAH",
